  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "Assume that \\(x\\) is a positive real number. Which is equivalent to \\[\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}}\\,?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x^{\\frac{1}{6}}\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)",
    "C": "\\(x^{\\frac{3}{8}}\\)",
    "D": "\\(x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)",
    "E": "\\(x\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(x>0\\), its square root is real and satisfies \\((\\sqrt{x})^2=x\\). Thus the expression inside the cube root is a perfect cube:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}}\n=\\sqrt[3]{(\\sqrt{x})^3}\n=\\sqrt{x}\n=x^{1/2}.\n\\]\nTaking a cube root undoes cubing a real number. The equivalent expression is therefore \\(\\boxed{x^{1/2}}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
